{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1443220-scenarios-abilities","id":1443220,"title":"Scenarios Abilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-09T00:04:33-07:00","id":1443220,"title":"Scenarios Abilities","content":"As player and SG, I noticed that many people tends to run combats in Scion (even today, with so many alternatives for maps on the web) more simplistic like &quot;I attack that dude&quot;/&quot;I dodge&quot;. And, imho, that is a waste. The system provides some nice rules to make things more interesting, Stunts for attack and defense, cover, armor, etc. So, I initially thought about writing a Nexus supplement with &quot;Tags&quot; a fight scenario may have. Things like: <i><b>Crowded</b></i>: If you Roll Away a ranged attack, another person (probably an innocent bystander) is hit instead; <i><b>Windy</b></i>: Throwing attacks have increased difficulty, etc... But that would be lame, and probably would more hinder than help. One more thing to everyone have in mind, and create the mindset like&quot;if it's not stated in the rules that a wet terrain conducts eletricity, so it doesn't&quot;. Also, I have no idea of how many of these Tags a scenario should have. Probably, like Antagonists, not a precise number, but &quot;enough&quot;. <br /> <br /> So my suggestion is to everyone, when SGing, take a moment to describe the scenario and make clear things like: &quot;What covers the characters (of both sides) can use?&quot; &quot;What are interesting things around people may use?&quot; &quot;There are some Stunts that should be favored of hindered by circunstances?&quot; (like: it would be difficult to use Roll Away when fighting in a van).<br /> <br /> So, I'm listing here what I can think and be free to add your own:<ul><li><b>Civilian: </b>There are innocent people around. Missed attacks (by any side) may hit them.</li> <li><b>Rainy: </b>It's... wet. Some eletronics things may not work, eletricity may be a problem, and any movement action has a chance to make you prone.</li> <li><b>Mist: </b>Shoot and Throwing attacks get +1 Difficulty.</li> <li><b>Dense Vegetation: </b>A valid example of Dificult Terrain (?).</li> <li><b>Noisy </b>(loud music, explosions, heavy machinery, etc.): It's hard (maybe impossible) to communicate by voice.</li> <li><b>Fiery</b>: There are points on fire in the scenario (thinking about a building on fire or a volcano eruption)... and they probably hurt.</li> <li><b>Chaotic</b>: Lots of stuff flying around. Poltergheist-y or maybe a hurricane. (Chaos Purview makes you immune, but well...)</li> <li><b>Explosives</b>: Well, there are explosives around for some reason, so a shot or a fire can make things go boom.</li> <li><b>Dark</b>: It's impossible to make ranged attacks without help.</li> <li><b>Holy Ground:</b> Some places are sacred to some pantheons or Gods. Simply announce an attack in there may be considered as an offense to some more sensible people.</li> </ul>Probably, Terra Incognitae and Overworlds have their own rules about how the Physics in there would work. But these are just some examples of how you can make things more interesting without to make the system too heavy to roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T01:22:57-07:00","id":1443224,"title":"","content":"Very interesting ideas. Usually when I prepare a scene in a unusual environment (by that I mean, not free space) I make notes about barriers (including difficulty to cross them) and conditions in the field (noise, smell, indirect damage, etc).<br /> The idea of adding tags to the fields makes it easier as you can describe easily the field rules wise and you may have some additional ideas while taking a look in the list (\u201coh yes, the thrash containers certainly smell bad! How could I forget to add that\u201d or \u201cthe avenue is just behind this wall, certainly the noise is enough to make it hard to listen something\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}